#. Tag: title
#: using-setup-album.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Album Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: using-setup-album.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid "Icon-View Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first series of settings on the left side of this view permit to "
"customize the technical information to show below the album icon-view "
"thumbnail, as the filename, the file size, the creation date, the image "
"dimensions, and the aspect ratio."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that <guilabel>Show file modification date</guilabel> option show the "
"file modification date only if it's different than <guilabel>Show camera "
"creation date</guilabel>. This option is useful to identify quickly which "
"items have been modified."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the right side, the options permit to customize other properties to show "
"over and below the album icon-view thumbnail, as the file mime-type, the "
"title, the caption, and the labels."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Show rotation overlay buttons</guilabel> option show overlay "
"buttons over the image thumbnail to be able to process left or right image "
"rotation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Show fullscreen overlay button</guilabel> option show an "
"overlay button over the image thumbnail to open it in fullscreen mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Show Geolocation Indicator</guilabel> option show an icon over "
"the image thumbnail if item has geolocation information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "An example of album icon-view item is given below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the bottom side of this settings panel, you can tune the behavior of icon-"
"view item with user actions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Thumbnail click action</guilabel> option permit to choose what "
"should happen when you click on a thumbnail. Two settings are avaialble: "
"<guilabel>Show embedded view</guilabel> to display image in preview mode "
"(F3) or <guilabel>Start image editor</guilabel> to open image in a separated "
"window (F4)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Icon View font</guilabel> option permit to select the font "
"used to display text in icon-views."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Use large thumbnail size for high screen resolution</guilabel> "
"option render icon-view with large thumbnail size, for example in case of 4K "
"monitor is used. By default this option is turned off and the maximum "
"thumbnail size is limited to 256x256 pixels. When this option is enabled, "
"thumbnail size can be extended to 512x512 pixels. This option will store "
"more data in thumbnail database and will use more system memory. &digikam; "
"needs to be restarted to take effect, and <link linkend=\"tool-maintenance-"
"features-thumbs\">Rebuild Thumbnails</link> option from Maintenance tool "
"needs to be processed over whole collections."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: using-setup-album.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "Folder View Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These settings permit to customize the album tree-view. The <guilabel>Tree "
"View thumbnail size</guilabel> option configure the size in pixels of the "
"Tree View thumbnails in &digikam;'s sidebars. Use large value for HiDPI "
"screen. The <guilabel>Tree View font</guilabel> option set the font used to "
"display text in Tree Views. The option <guilabel>Show a count of items in "
"Tree Views</guilabel> will display along the album name the number of icon-"
"view items inside."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: using-setup-album.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "Album View Preview Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Instead to open the image in editor, the &digikam; preview mode (<keycap>F3</"
"keycap>) will embedded the large image view inside the main window. The goal "
"to this view is to be faster than image editor, to be able to review the "
"list of current images quickly. Depending of your computer features, you can "
"customize the better way to load image to preview. Raw files can be "
"processed differently, as this kind of container can require long "
"computation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When option <guilabel>Embedded view zoomed to the original image size</"
"guilabel> is not turned on, preview mode will not zoom the embedded view to "
"the original image size."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-setup-album.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When option <guilabel>Show icons and text over preview</guilabel> is not "
"turned on, preview mode will not show icons and text over the image preview."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: using-setup-album.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "Album View Full-Screen Settings"
msgstr ""

